figures.caption_en:
Figure 1: The left panel displays a percentage bar plot illustrating the optical nuclear classification of the complete sample of 38 ULIRGs. The right panel shows a scatter plot of \(q_{
u}\) versus \(\log L_{60\,\mu{m}}\) for the 38 ULIRGs. Filled points indicate the 13 sources from the first phase of this study, taken from Nandi et al. (2021) . The green line denotes the average \(q_{
u}\) value of 1.88 for the 38 sources in our sample, while the red line marks the \(q_{
u}=2.34\) threshold from Yun et al. (2001) . Sources below this threshold exhibit characteristics of radio excess, whereas those above the threshold indicate infrared excess.

figures.caption_zh:
图1：左图显示了38个ULIRGs完整样本的光学核分类的百分比条形图。右图显示了38个ULIRGs的 \(q_{
u}\) 与 \(\log L_{60\,\mu{m}}\) 的散点图。实心点表示来自本研究第一阶段的13个源，取自Nandi等人（2021）。绿线表示我们样本中38个源的平均 \(q_{
u}\) 值1.88，而红线标记了Yun等人（2001）的 \(q_{
u}=2.34\) 阈值。低于此阈值的源表现出射电过量的特征，而高于阈值的源则表示红外过量。
